# XingAI foundation (all products)

Applies to every `xingai-*` repo and `*.xingai.app` product app. Read `AGENTS.md` first (includes Product Upgrade Rule + Meal/Cook/Invest examples). For UI implementation details, use skill **`xingai-web-design`** (`~/.cursor/skills/xingai-web-design/`).

**Invest AI** also follows `xingai-invest-ai/.cursor/rules/decision-cache-boundary.mdc` (worker owns decisions; FastAPI read-only).

---

## Mobile-first (required)

- Design **320–430px usable width first**; add `sm:` / `lg:` only when scaling up — never desktop-first shrink.
- **Touch targets** ≥ 44×44 CSS px; adequate gap between tappable controls.
- **Safe areas:** `env(safe-area-inset-*)` on fixed top/bottom chrome and main `padding-bottom`.
- **Single-column default** on base styles; no dense multi-column tables on phone without scroll or fold.
- **Performance:** primary decision content before decorative chrome in DOM order.
- Do **not** fake OS status bars in the DOM.

---

## Navigation chrome (required)

Every shipped product surface must expose the **same nav destinations** across form factors. Labels are product-specific; **pattern is not optional**.

| Surface | Mobile (`< lg` / ~576px) | Desktop (`lg+`) |
|---------|--------------------------|-----------------|
| **Top bar** | Sticky: menu · brand/title · **language + theme** (profile if applicable) | Sticky top bar; same controls visible or reachable |
| **Side menu** | **Sheet/drawer** from hamburger; full nav + settings fallback | **Same sheet** from menu **or** persistent sidebar — repo must pick one and stay consistent |
| **Footer bar** | **Fixed bottom tab bar** for primary destinations (`lg:hidden`) | No bottom tab bar |
| **Footer links** | Legal + help in drawer footer and/or page footer | Same legal links in site footer |

Rules:

1. **Never hide language or theme on mobile** unless the **side drawer** repeats them.
2. Long titles: truncate (`ellipsis`); narrow screens may hide logo before truncating title.
3. Main content `padding-bottom` ≥ bottom nav height + safe area when bottom nav exists.
4. Mark unreleased nav items **Soon** (disabled + toast) — do not ship empty routes.
5. Do **not** expose internal version labels (V1/V2) in user-facing nav or titles.

**Reference:** `xingai-dot-app` → `Header`, `MobileNavDrawer`, `MobileBottomNav`. Product apps → Cook/Meal `MobileChrome` (top + sheet + bottom nav on mobile).

