## Language — EN / 中文 / 한국어 (required)

Locale codes in code: **`en`**, **`zh`** (中文), **`ko`** (한국어).

- All **new user-facing strings** go through the repo i18n layer (e.g. `messages.js`, `translations.ts`, locale provider) — no hard-coded UI copy in components.
- **Persist** locale (cookie and/or `localStorage`); re-apply on load before paint when possible (`i18n-boot` pattern in UX mocks).
- **Marketing site (`xingai-dot-app`):** locale in **URL path** (`/`, `/zh/…`, `/ko/…`); switcher changes path, not cookie-only. `hreflang` + per-locale canonical.
- **Product apps:** locale in UI + prompt/output language for AI routes; document supported locales in README.
- Legal pages and disclaimers: **all three locales** before calling legal “done”.
- Optional fourth locale (e.g. `es`) is product-specific — never replace en/zh/ko.

---

## Theme — light / dark (required)

- Support **`light` and `dark`** on every product app and marketing page.
- Set theme on `<html data-theme="…">` (static UX) or `next-themes` + `.dark` (Next.js apps).
- **No flash:** inline init script or `next-themes` `defaultTheme` + `enableSystem` as repo convention dictates.
- Update **`theme-color`** meta when theme changes.
- Demo/marketing imagery: provide **light + dark** pairs where screenshots are theme-dependent (`ThemedImage` on dot-app).
- Use product **oklch tokens** from repo `globals.css` / `tokens.css` — no random hex primary colors.

---

## Legal protection (required)

Every **public** `*.xingai.app` product must link to (host locally or on `xingai.app`):

| Page | Slug | Purpose |
|------|------|---------|
| **Privacy Policy** | `/legal/privacy` | Data collection, AI usage, cookies |
| **Terms of Service** | `/legal/terms` | Use of product, limitations |
| **Disclaimer** | `/legal/disclaimer` | Not professional advice; travel/style/invest suggestions |

Also:

- **Footer** on marketing site and product apps: links to all three (+ contact if available).
- AI lifestyle/travel products: state **suggestions only; verify before booking/action**.
- Invest: risk-first disclaimer; no return promises.
- New features with payments: mention refunds/support channel in Terms before launch.

**Reference:** `xingai-dot-app/app/i18n/legal-content.ts`, `LegalDocumentShell.tsx`.

---

## SEO (required)

Before calling a product route “shipped”:

- **`metadataBase`**, unique **title** + **description** per route.
- **Canonical URL** per page (locale-aware on marketing site).
- **Open Graph + Twitter** card (`og:title`, `og:description`, `og:image` — use product screenshot or branded OG, not favicon alone).
- **`sitemap.xml`** including all public locales and main routes.
- **`robots.txt`** allowing public pages; `Sitemap:` directive.
- **`lang`** on `<html>` matches active locale.
- Internal links respect active locale (no `/apps` when user is on `/zh/apps`).

Marketing checklist: `xingai-dot-app/docs/seo-aeo-checklist.md`.

---

## AEO — AI answer engines (required)

- **`llms.txt`** at product root or `public/` — plain-language summary: what the product does, primary URL, main user flow, supported languages, disclaimer one-liner.
- Homepage or product landing: **short factual FAQ** (3–5 Q&A) aligned with on-page copy.
- **JSON-LD** where applicable: `SoftwareApplication` on product/marketing app pages; `FAQPage` on marketing home; `Organization` / `WebSite` on dot-app.
- FAQ/schema answers: **factual**, name real domains (`cook.xingai.app`, etc.), no hype.
- Keep **`llms.txt` and FAQ in sync** when positioning or main flow changes.

---

## Pre-ship checklist (agent)

When adding or shipping a user-facing surface:

- [ ] Mobile layout verified at ~375px; safe areas; bottom nav clearance
- [ ] Top + side drawer + bottom nav (mobile) wired; desktop top chrome
- [ ] en / zh / ko strings complete for new copy
- [ ] Light + dark theme; no unreadable contrast
- [ ] Footer links: Privacy, Terms, Disclaimer
- [ ] `generateMetadata` (or static `seo-config.js`) + canonical + OG
- [ ] `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, `llms.txt` updated if routes changed
- [ ] No internal version labels in UI

